    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.notify\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nI was recently making some changes to my config and noticed that, when `nvim` is started with `-M` (or anything else that turns off the global value of 'modifiable'), the first notification sends 'mini.notify' into an endless busy loop. The `nvim` server process sits at about half a CPU core indefinitely on my machine, and the notification is never shown.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n    - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n   Populate it with the following content:\n\n    ```lua\n    -- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\n    local mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\n    local clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim', mini_path }\n    vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n    -- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\n    vim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\n    require('mini.deps').setup()\n\n    -- Add extra setup steps needed to reproduce the behavior\n    require('mini.notify').setup()\n\n    -- Count how often `SafeState` fires\n    _G.safestate_count = 0\n    vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('SafeState', {\n      callback = function() _G.safestate_count = _G.safestate_count + 1 end,\n    })\n    ```\n\n3. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim -M` (note the `-M`).\n   Wait for all dependencies to install.\n\n4. Execute `:lua MiniNotify.add('Hello')`. No notification window appears. Wait a couple of seconds, then execute `:lua =_G.safestate_count`: it prints tens of thousands and keeps growing on each check. Meanwhile `top` shows the `nvim --embed` server process at ~50% CPU. Without `-M`, the notification appears and the count stays small.",
