        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hello @macintacos \n\nThanks for the issue! I can reproduce. Some observations:\n\nAlthough I only observe an [abnormal](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/561751e839b99a4baca36b9d963166b66d2536a6/lua/mini/notify.lua#L457) `_G.safestate_count` with `mini.notify`, the 'M' flag also affects for example `mini.pick`. \n\nMiniPick appears but shows no options with this command: `:lua vim.ui.select({'abc', 'def'}, {}, function() end)`\n\nAlso affected: `mini.files`:\n\n```txt\n... Vim(lua):E5108: Lua: [string \":lua\"]:1: Buffer is not 'modifiable' ...\n```\n\nWhen using `vim.pack`, doing a `:packupdate`:\n\n```txt\n/usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/pack.lua:1326: Buffer is not 'modifiable'\n```\n\n\nIn general, this flag seems to be very problematic for plugins that \"own\" a special buffer and window.\n\nCan you specify when you need this flag in your workflow?\n\n\n\n",
